chunks.content:
The .card-inset is a rounded rectangle that fills the page. Key CSS properties:
- background: var(--navy) (or adapted color)
- border-radius: 12px
- min-height: calc(11in - 1.5in) — fills the printable area
- display: flex; flex-direction: column — enables flex layout
- padding: calc(2.5rem * var(--s)) calc(2.75rem * var(--s)) calc(2.25rem * var(--s))
- color: var(--white) (or adapted color)
- box-sizing: border-box

One child element gets flex:1 to fill remaining vertical space (usually a grid or stats section).

Required media queries:
@media print { .PREFIX .card-inset { min-height:auto; } }
@media (max-width:700px) { /* collapse grids to single-column, reduce padding */ }

Every proposal page block must include two media queries:

1. @media print { .PREFIX .card-inset { min-height: auto; } } — relaxes the fixed height for printing so content flows naturally.

2. @media (max-width: 700px) { } — collapses grid layouts to single column, reduces padding, adjusts font sizes for mobile viewing. Example:
@media (max-width:700px) {
  .PREFIX .card-inset { padding: calc(1.5rem * var(--s)); }
  .PREFIX .grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  .PREFIX .two-col { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
}

Two-column info boxes use CSS grid for side-by-side content blocks. Good for feature comparisons, service highlights, contact details.

CSS pattern:
.PREFIX .two-col { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: calc(1rem * var(--s)); }
.PREFIX .info-box { background: var(--navy-lt); border-radius: 8px; padding: calc(1.15rem * var(--s)) calc(1.25rem * var(--s)); }
.PREFIX .info-box h3 { font-size: calc(12pt * var(--s)); font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 calc(0.4rem * var(--s)) 0; }
.PREFIX .info-box p { font-size: calc(10pt * var(--s)); line-height: 1.55; margin: 0; }

Collapses to single column at 700px via the responsive media query.

Card grids display service breakdowns or plan comparisons. Each card has a colored top border accent.

CSS pattern:
.PREFIX .grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: calc(0.85rem * var(--s)); flex: 1; align-content: center; }
.PREFIX .card { background: var(--navy-lt); border-radius: 8px; padding: calc(1rem * var(--s)) calc(1.15rem * var(--s)); border-top: 3px solid var(--teal); display: flex; flex-direction: column; }

For 3-column: grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
For 2x2 with flex fill: the .grid gets flex:1 so it stretches to fill remaining card-inset space, and align-content:center keeps items vertically centered.

Circular stat indicators using CSS border trick. Good for compliance rates, savings percentages, coverage stats.

CSS pattern:
.PREFIX .stats { display: flex; justify-content: space-around; padding: calc(1.5rem * var(--s)) 0; }
.PREFIX .stat { text-align: center; }
.PREFIX .stat .ring { width: 100px; height: 100px; border-radius: 50%; border: 5px solid var(--navy-lt); border-top-color: var(--teal); display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; margin: 0 auto calc(0.5rem * var(--s)); }
.PREFIX .stat .ring span { font-size: calc(18pt * var(--s)); font-weight: 700; }
.PREFIX .stat .label { font-size: calc(9pt * var(--s)); color: var(--off); }

Accent-colored box for key quotes, highlights, or calls to action.

CSS pattern:
.PREFIX .callout { background: var(--teal-bg); border-radius: 6px; padding: calc(0.75rem * var(--s)) calc(1rem * var(--s)); margin-top: calc(0.75rem * var(--s)); }
.PREFIX .callout p { font-size: calc(10pt * var(--s)); line-height: 1.55; margin: 0; color: var(--off); }
.PREFIX .callout strong { color: var(--white); }

Can also be used with a left border accent:
.PREFIX .callout-bar { border-left: 3px solid var(--teal); padding-left: calc(1rem * var(--s)); }

The TITLE section is the first thing the prospect sees. It should include:
- PSP name (use {{PSP_NAME}} token)
- A headline like 'Benefits Administration Proposal' or custom title
- Prospect name via {{PROSPECT_NAME}}
- Agent info via {{AGENT_NAME}} and optionally {{AGENT_EMAIL}}
- Date via {{DATE_CREATED}}

Title pages can range from minimal/elegant (centered text, lots of whitespace) to graphic-heavy (colored backgrounds, accent shapes, grid layout). The card-inset pattern works well for both — adjust colors, font sizes, and spacing density.

Brand-adaptive title pages use {{PRIMARY_COLOR}} and {{ACCENT_COLOR}} in CSS variables so they automatically match any PSP's branding.

A clean white COBRA overview page adapts the card-inset to light theme:

.cobra1 { --s:1; --primary: {{PRIMARY_COLOR}}; --accent: {{ACCENT_COLOR}}; --bg: #ffffff; --text: #333333; --muted: #6c757d; --card-bg: #f0f4f8; font-family: 'Source Sans 3', sans-serif; }
.cobra1 .card-inset { background: var(--bg); color: var(--text); border-radius: 12px; border: 1px solid #dee2e6; }

Structure: title with colored accent bar, intro paragraph, 2-column info boxes describing COBRA services, a bullet list of compliance features, and a callout box with regulatory note.

This demonstrates that the card-inset can be white — just change the background and color variables. The accent color comes from {{PRIMARY_COLOR}} for brand-adaptive styling.

A brand-adaptive title page uses merge tokens in CSS variables so it automatically matches any PSP's brand colors:

.title1 { --s:1; --primary: {{PRIMARY_COLOR}}; --accent: {{ACCENT_COLOR}}; --white: #fff; font-family: 'Source Sans 3', sans-serif; }
.title1 .card-inset { background: var(--primary); color: var(--white); }
.title1 .accent-line { height: 4px; background: var(--accent); border-radius: 2px; width: 80px; margin: 1rem auto; }

Structure: centered layout with {{PSP_NAME}} as main heading, accent divider line, 'Benefits Administration Proposal' subtitle, {{PROSPECT_NAME}} in a slightly smaller weight, agent info block at bottom with {{AGENT_NAME}} and {{DATE_CREATED}}.

Because colors come from merge tokens, this same HTML works for every PSP without modification.
